course: dictionary
lesson: 11830
title: Blackened: dark, spicy and damaged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can change its meaning, but the words around it show you which meaning is right. Blackened is a past form of the verb blacken, so it often describes something that has already changed. «The walls were blackened by the smoke from the fire.» The smoke came first, and then the walls were dark. So blackened means made black or dark.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Chef Ray cooked blackened fish in a very hot pan with spices.» The words cooked, pan and spices tell you that blackened is a cooking word here. The outside of the fish turned dark, but it is still food to eat.
explain: Some words move from objects to people. «Her spiteful lie blackened her friend's name at school.» Nobody painted the name black. To blacken someone's name means to damage how other people think of them by saying bad things about them.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence. Ask: does this still make sense? If the sentence fits the clues, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Blacken is a verb, and blackened is its past form. It can also be used as an adjective, like a blackened wall.
fact: «Blackened» means made black or dark, for example by fire, smoke or dirt.
fact: «Blackened fish» is a spicy dish cooked in a very hot pan, so the outside turns dark.
fact: Blackened food is a style of Cajun cooking from Louisiana, USA.
fact: To blacken someone's name means to damage their reputation by saying bad things about them.
exercise: «The walls were blackened by the smoke from the fire.» What does blackened mean here? | Cleaned until they shone | *Made black or dark by smoke | Painted bright white | Covered in snow
exercise: Maya said Sam had cheated, and the lie blackened his name. What does blackened mean here? | *Damaged how people think of him | Wrote his name in black ink | Made his name easier to read | Hid his name under a sheet
exercise: «Chef Ray cooked blackened fish in a very hot pan with spices.» How was the fish cooked? | Frozen in ice for a whole week | *In a very hot pan with spices, so the outside turned dark | Boiled in plain water for hours | Left out in the sun to dry
test: «The old stone church was blackened by a hundred years of coal smoke.» What does blackened tell us? | The stone had been painted pink | *Coal smoke had made the stone dark | The church was newly built and very clean
test: Which word is the past form of the verb blacken? | Blackening | Blackens | *Blackened | Black
exam: Which sentence uses blackened to mean damaged someone's reputation? | «The sea was blackened by the storm clouds at dusk.» | «The chimney blackened after a winter of coal fires.» | «The fire blackened the roof of the barn.» | *«Her spiteful rumours blackened her friend's name at school.»
